MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: b8cb648fdf2cd024d97f20a78acfcd4c, type: 3}
  m_Name: PracticalGuide_Cylinder_Azm
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::VirtualLab.Azm.Core.PracticalGuide_Azm
  title: 'Vernier Calipers: Solid Cylinder (Exp 1.1 and 1.2)'
  aim: 'Exp 1.1: find the area of cross-section of a solid cylinder.

    Exp 1.2:
    find its volume.

    Both by measuring its diameter and length with vernier
    calipers.'
  description: Vernier calipers measure lengths to a hundredth of a centimetre. The
    sliding vernier scale next to the main scale lets you read the fraction of a
    millimetre between two main-scale marks.
  apparatus:
  - Vernier calipers
  - Solid metal cylinder
  whatYouMeasure: "The least count and the zero error of the calipers, then the diameter
    D of the cylinder three times and its length L three times. From their means:
    r = D/2, the area of cross-section A = \u03C0r\xB2 and the volume V = \u03C0r\xB2L."
  procedure:
  - "Find the least count: LC = smallest main-scale division \xF7 number of vernier
    divisions."
  - Close the jaws gently and find the zero error and the zero correction.
  - "Grip the cylinder across between the outside jaws. Read the main scale M and
    the vernier division n that coincides: Y = M + n \xD7 LC, then apply the zero
    correction. Repeat at three places."
  - Grip the cylinder lengthwise and measure its length L the same way, three times.
  - "Find the mean D and the mean L, then r = D/2, A = \u03C0r\xB2 and V = \u03C0r\xB2L."
  - Record your results.
  formulas:
  - "Least count LC = smallest main-scale division \xF7 number of vernier divisions"
  - "Fraction X = n \xD7 LC;  observed value Y = M + X"
  - "Zero correction ZC = \u2212(zero error);  corrected value = Y + ZC"
  - "Radius r = D / 2;  area of cross-section A = \u03C0r\xB2"
  - "Volume V = \u03C0r\xB2L"
  precautions:
  - text: Close the jaws gently.
    why: Pressing hard can bend the jaws and change every reading.
  - text: Apply the zero correction.
    why: If the vernier 0 is not on the main-scale 0 with the jaws closed, every
      reading is off by the same amount.
  - text: Both jaws should touch the cylinder.
    why: A gap makes the reading too large; squeezing tilts the jaws.
  - text: Take readings at different places.
    why: A real cylinder is not perfectly even, so the mean of several readings is
      more reliable.
  observationTable: "For L\u2081\u2013L\u2083 and D\u2081\u2013D\u2083: main-scale
    reading M, vernier division n, fraction X = n \xD7 LC, observed value Y = M +
    X, corrected value Y + ZC (all in cm). The least count, zero error and zero correction
    are written above the table."
